(begin-tx "UTIL-08 — UEV_HibernationFees: bounds, then a divisibility nobody would guess")
(env-gasmodel "table")(env-gaslimit 10000000)(env-gas 0)
;;==== UTIL-08 — UEV_HibernationFees: bounds, then a divisibility nobody would guess · 01 · namespace ==== 
(print "--- [UTIL-08 — UEV_HibernationFees: bounds, then a divisibility nobody would guess · 01 · namespace] ---")
(namespace "ouronet-ns")
(print "--- [UTIL-08 · 01 · peak/decay] ---")
;;Two enforces. The first folds SIX bounds into one message; the second is a scaled-integer
;;divisibility check that is easy to miss entirely -- peak and decay can both be perfectly valid
;;and the pair still be refused because peak*10000 does not divide by decay*10000.
;;
;;This function carries an audit scar worth keeping visible: its @doc records finding #10M/M1,
;;a stray malformed 7th predicate `(= () 0.0)` comparing Pact's unit value against 0.0 -- always
;;false, so the enforce rejected EVERY input. It was deleted 2026-08-17. The happy-path
;;assertion below is what would have caught it; there was no such assertion at the time.
;;==== UTIL-08 — UEV_HibernationFees: bounds, then a divisibility nobody would guess · 02 · let / invocation ==== 
(print "--- [UTIL-08 — UEV_HibernationFees: bounds, then a divisibility nobody would guess · 02 · let / invocation] ---")
(let
    (
        (ref-U|ATS:module{UtilityAtsV3} U|ATS)
    )
    (map print
        [
            ;;HAPPY PATH -- the assertion the #10M debris would have failed.
            (expect "<<UTIL-08>> a valid (peak, decay) pair is accepted"
                true (!= "" (format "{}" [(ref-U|ATS::UEV_HibernationFees 1.0 0.5)])))
            ;;the six-way fold, one message, three different causes shown.
            (expect-failure "<<UTIL-08>> a zero peak is refused"
                "Invalid Hibernation Fees" (ref-U|ATS::UEV_HibernationFees 0.0 0.5))
            (expect-failure "<<UTIL-08>> ...a peak over the 800.0 ceiling, same message"
                "Invalid Hibernation Fees" (ref-U|ATS::UEV_HibernationFees 800.0001 0.5))
            (expect-failure "<<UTIL-08>> ...and a decay of 1.0, which must be strictly below 1"
                "Invalid Hibernation Fees" (ref-U|ATS::UEV_HibernationFees 1.0 1.0))
            ;;THE SECOND GUARD. Both values are individually legal -- peak 1.0 is in range at 4dp,
            ;;decay 0.3 is in (0,1) at 4dp -- and the pair is still refused, because
            ;;10000 mod 3000 = 1000. A caller reading only the bounds would never predict this.
            (expect-failure "<<UTIL-08>> two individually-legal values can still fail the scaled division"
                "Invalid Hibernation Fees via Scaled Division"
                (ref-U|ATS::UEV_HibernationFees 1.0 0.3))
        ]
    )
    ""
)
(commit-tx)
;;|| NEXT >
